{
  "name": "uft_shared_resume_control",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "steps": [
    {
      "comment": "Control for uft_shared_resume (issue #11): identical scene, fix withheld. Roles: 0 = anchor, 1 = member, -1 = neither, -2 = nothing to report.",
      "type": "SetTime",
      "args": {
        "hour": "9"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "SetTerrain",
      "args": {
        "def": "Concrete",
        "width": "20",
        "height": "20"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PlaceThings",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench",
        "layout": "cells",
        "cells": "-4,0; 4,0",
        "rot": "North"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgClaimBenches",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgLinkBenches",
      "args": {
        "def": "HandTailoringBench",
        "limit": "2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_group_size",
        "expectedValue": "2",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_redirect_installed",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The control. Same scene, with the three issue-#11 patches withheld for the rest of the process, asserting vanilla's outcome. It proves the probes in uft_shared_resume can see the difference. RedirectInstalled stays 1 (the transpiler ran at startup), which is what still lets the order into the list. Run this scenario on its own, never in a suite: Harmony state outlives a scenario, and a failure before the restore step at the end leaves the patches off.",
      "type": "WbgWithholdPatches",
      "args": {
        "classes": "Patch_WorkGiver_DoBill_FinishUftJob, Patch_HaulAIUtility_PawnCanAutomaticallyHaulFast, Patch_UnfinishedThing_BoundWorkTable"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Negative path first, on the empty list: bills that genuinely cannot be shared still bounce off AddBill, now that they share IsShareableBill with the ones that can. Lifter is a Bill_ProductionMech (gestation), ResurrectLightMech a Bill_ResurrectMech. Both Biotech; ifPresent logs a skip on a machine without it.",
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "Lifter",
        "expect": "refused",
        "ifPresent": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "ResurrectLightMech",
        "expect": "refused",
        "ifPresent": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_bills_visible_at_second_bench",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The positive half of the gate: a Bill_ProductionWithUft goes into the shared list and is visible from the member.",
      "type": "WbgTryAddBill",
      "args": {
        "recipe": "Make_Apparel_BasicShirt",
        "expect": "added"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_bills_visible_at_second_bench",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgSpawnStack",
      "args": {
        "def": "Cloth",
        "count": "75",
        "cell": "0,-3"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgSpawnStack",
      "args": {
        "def": "Steel",
        "count": "10",
        "cell": "0,-6",
        "role": "control"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgMakeStockpile",
      "args": {
        "from": "-2,4",
        "to": "2,6",
        "allow": "Steel, UnfinishedApparel"
      },
      "comment": "Accepts only the control steel and the unfinished item, so the hauler's window is spent on the two things under test rather than the fixture colony's junk. Accepting the unfinished item is what makes 'left alone' a finding: the stockpile would take it."
    },
    {
      "type": "SpawnPawn",
      "args": {
        "kind": "Colonist",
        "count": "4",
        "faction": "player",
        "offset": "-3,-9",
        "spacing": "2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgAssignRoles",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "comment": "Phase 1: the member is busy, so the crafter starts the order at the anchor. The unfinished item appears there.",
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "member"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "900"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_crafter_job_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_count",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Interrupted: drafted mid-craft, the item stays on the anchor. Then the anchor becomes the busy one.",
      "type": "WbgDraft",
      "args": {
        "drafted": "true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgRememberUft",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "anchor"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Vanilla aims the resume job at the anchor — the busy bench — even though the member was the bench scanned.",
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_resume_target_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "The crafter cannot carry the item to the member without the redirect, so the hauler half of the control parks it there by hand.",
      "type": "WbgMoveUft",
      "args": {
        "to": "member"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgOccupyBench",
      "args": {
        "which": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_vanilla_guard",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_haulable",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_bound_table_at",
        "expectedValue": "0",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgCloseDebugLog",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "Select",
      "args": {
        "defName": "UnfinishedApparel",
        "count": "1"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "LookAt",
      "args": {
        "zoom": "13"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Wait",
      "args": {
        "frames": "20"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Screenshot",
      "args": {
        "fileName": "uft_parked_at_member_control.png",
        "hideUi": "false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgEnableWork",
      "args": {
        "role": "hauler",
        "workType": "Hauling"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "FastForward",
      "args": {
        "ticks": "5000"
      },
      "comment": "Long enough for a randomly generated hauler to finish carrying the leftover cloth as well as the control steel; 2500 ticks passed on one pawn and not on the next."
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgLogCrafter",
      "args": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_control_in_storage",
        "expectedValue": "1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Vanilla: the half-made shirt at the member read as litter and went to the stockpile.",
      "type": "Probe",
      "args": {
        "probeName": "wbg_uft_at",
        "expectedValue": "-1",
        "tolerance": "0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "WbgWithholdPatches",
      "args": {
        "classes": "Patch_WorkGiver_DoBill_FinishUftJob, Patch_HaulAIUtility_PawnCanAutomaticallyHaulFast, Patch_UnfinishedThing_BoundWorkTable",
        "restore": "true"
      }
    }
  ]
}
